# Project Rules

## General

- Always follow the existing project patterns, architecture, and design.
- Reuse existing patterns and conventions instead of introducing new ones.
- Do not invent names, structures, or patterns when an existing convention is available.
- Always ask if you have any doubt about a new feature or task. Never assume.

## Scope Control

- Only implement what is explicitly requested.
- Do not assume additional requirements or add related functionality.
- Do not modify unrelated files, features, or business logic.
- Make the minimum changes necessary to complete the task.
- Do not refactor or improve existing code unless it is required for the requested task.

## Change Approval

- If an additional change is necessary, always consult with me before making it.
- Before making an additional change, explain:
  - Why it is needed.
  - What it changes.
  - What benefit it provides.
- If there is any doubt whether a change is required, ask first.

## Recommendations

- If you identify a better approach, recommend it before changing the implementation.
- Clearly distinguish between:
  - Required change
  - Recommended improvement
  - Optional improvement
- A recommendation is not permission to change the code.